<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Designing your own style files>

  Whenever the standard <TeXmacs> style files are inadequate for a given
  purpose, it is possible to write your own style files. However, designing
  your own style file from scratch may be a complex task. For this reason, we
  recommend the reuse or customization of the standard <TeXmacs> style files
  and packages whenever possible. Consequently, it may be wise to read more
  about the <hlink|customization|../customize/customize.en.tm> of the
  <TeXmacs> style files and packages first.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|Look at an example|example.en.tm>

    <branch|Keyboard shortcuts for writing style
    files|../keyboard/style-kbd.en.tm>

    <branch|Important paths|paths.en.tm>
  </traverse>

